<!doctype html>
<html {% if request.design_mode %}class="shopify-design-mode"{% endif %} lang="{{ request.locale.iso_code }}">
<head>

  {%- comment -%}
  ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  layout/theme.liquid — Legendary Branding
  Branch: ui-redesign-2026
  Rewrite: 2026-05-22

  Load order (do not reorder without PSI testing):
    1.  <meta charset> — before anything else touches encoding
    2.  Preconnects + DNS-prefetch — warm origins before any resource fires
    3.  LCP image preload — fires at HTML head parse, earliest possible
    4.  Chaos Unleashed master — intercepts CFH before content_for_header
    5.  content_for_header capture + cfh_defer — app scripts deferred
    6.  dataLayer init (single, authoritative) — before GTM
    7.  GTM — async-injected after DOMContentLoaded, not render-blocking
    8.  Meta tags, SEO, hreflang, schema
    9.  Critical CSS inline — covers header + hero so first paint is correct
    10. Font preloads + @font-face
    11. Bebas Neue self-hosted font
    12. Theme flash prevention (localStorage read, zero network cost)
    13. CSS custom properties (theme variables, color schemes)
    14. Non-critical CSS — preload-swap (async)
    15. View transition opt-in (guarded — only when setting is active)
    16. Theme editor (design mode only)
    17. Module importmap + modulepreload hints (fetchpriority=low)
    18. lb-app-css-defer — catches runtime-injected app CSS
    19. lb-ghost-code-auditor
    20. lb-speculation-rules — prefetch/prerender on hover (Chrome 109+)
  ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  {%- endcomment -%}

  {%- comment -%}── 1. ENCODING ──────────────────────────────────────────────{%- endcomment -%}
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover">
  <meta name="theme-color" content="#000000" media="(prefers-color-scheme: dark)">
  <meta name="theme-color" content="#ffffff" media="(prefers-color-scheme: light)">

  {%- comment -%}── 2. PRECONNECTS ────────────────────────────────────────────
    Order matters: most latency-critical origins first.
    GTM is first because it injects GA4 + ad pixels — warming it early
    saves ~80ms on the first GTM payload. Shopify CDN second because
    it serves every asset (JS, CSS, fonts, images).
    Third-party pixels (FB, Pinterest, Snapchat) last — they load after
    idle so their preconnects are advisory, not critical-path.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://www.googletagmanager.com">
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://cdn.shopify.com" crossorigin>
  <link rel="dns-prefetch" href="https://www.google-analytics.com">
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://connect.facebook.net" crossorigin>
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://s.pinimg.com" crossorigin>
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://sc-static.net" crossorigin>
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://checkout.shopify.com" crossorigin>
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://static.klaviyo.com" crossorigin>
  <link rel="dns-prefetch" href="//connect.facebook.net">
  <link rel="dns-prefetch" href="//s.pinimg.com">
  <link rel="dns-prefetch" href="//sc-static.net">
  <link rel="dns-prefetch" href="//checkout.shopify.com">
  <link rel="dns-prefetch" href="//static.klaviyo.com">

  {%- comment -%}── 3. LCP PRELOAD ────────────────────────────────────────────
    seo-preconnect runs here to warm the CDN before the preload resolves.
    lb-hero-lcp-preload fires immediately after — browser starts fetching
    the hero poster before the parser reaches the hero section (~5-6s later
    on slow mobile without this).
    Scope: homepage only (template.name == 'index').
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- render 'seo-preconnect' -%}
  {%- render 'lb-hero-lcp-preload' -%}
  {%- render 'lb-collection-lcp-preload' -%}
  {%- render 'lb-article-lcp-preload' -%}

  {%- comment -%}── 4 + 5. CHAOS UNLEASHED ────────────────────────────────────
    Must render BEFORE content_for_header is emitted so Chaos can
    intercept and defer app CSS/JS injected by Shopify into CFH.
    cfh_defer receives the raw CFH string as a parameter — it parses it
    server-side and re-emits only non-blocking resources.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- render 'chaos_unleashed_master' -%}
  {%- capture Chaos_Raw_CFH -%}{{ content_for_header }}{%- endcapture -%}
  {%- render 'chaos_unleashed_cfh_defer', raw_cfh: Chaos_Raw_CFH -%}

  {%- comment -%}── 6. DATALAYER (single authoritative init) ─────────────────
    Must exist before GTM and before any app script pushes events.
    Zero network cost — pure JS array declaration.
    Single init here replaces the three separate declarations that
    existed in the previous version.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <script>window.dataLayer=window.dataLayer||[];</script>

  {%- comment -%}── 7. GOOGLE TAG MANAGER ────────────────────────────────────────
    GTM loading strategy:

    — Product / cart / collection pages: load on DOMContentLoaded.
      These pages start conversion funnel events immediately on user
      interaction (add_to_cart, begin_checkout). GTM must be ready
      before the first click — idle-load risks missing early funnel
      events on fast shoppers, producing (not set) source attribution.

    — All other pages: 3-tier idle strategy (requestIdleCallback →
      4s fallback → interaction backstop). Safe to defer because no
      conversion events fire until the user navigates to a product.

    Tier 1 — requestIdleCallback: fires when the main thread is free
    Tier 2 — 4s hard fallback: guarantees GTM loads on slow devices
    Tier 3 — user interaction backstop: loads on first intent

    The noscript <iframe> fallback is still in <body> (required by
    Google). The preconnect at step 2 warms the GTM origin.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    Analytics suppression flag — set server-side from Shopify request context.
    GTM must NOT load (and dataLayer must not seed gtm.js) in any non-customer
    context, otherwise the theme editor / preview / app-callback renders
    pollute GA4 sessions and split attribution (the (direct)/(none) noise that
    inflated Shopify sessions far above GA4's real customer sessions).

    Suppressed contexts:
      - request.design_mode      → Theme editor live preview
      - request.visual_preview_mode → Theme library "Preview" + checkout editor
    Client-side, the bootstrap additionally suppresses when the URL carries
    preview/debug params that Shopify and apps append in non-customer renders.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <script>
  window.__lbSuppressAnalytics = {% if request.design_mode or request.visual_preview_mode %}true{% else %}false{% endif %};
  </script>
  <script>
  (function(){
    var INTERACTION_EVENTS=['mousedown','touchstart','keydown','scroll','click'];
    // Client-side suppression backstop: preview/debug/sandbox URL params that
    // appear only in non-customer renders. Keeps real customer tracking intact
    // because these params never appear on organic/paid customer landings.
    function isNoiseContext(){
      if(window.__lbSuppressAnalytics) return true;
      try{
        // Web pixel sandbox / app callback renders run cross-origin in an iframe.
        if(window.top !== window.self) return true;
        var qs = window.location.search;
        if(!qs) return false;
        var NOISE = ['preview_theme_id','_ab','_fd','_sc','_ssvprev','webPixelDebug','webPixelsManagerSandbox','_bt','pb=0'];
        for(var i=0;i<NOISE.length;i++){ if(qs.indexOf(NOISE[i]) !== -1) return true; }
      }catch(e){ return true; } // cross-origin access throw → we're framed → suppress
      return false;
    }
    if(isNoiseContext()){ window.__lbSuppressAnalytics = true; return; }
    function loadGTM(){
      if(window.__gtmLoaded)return;
      if(window.__lbSuppressAnalytics)return;
      window.__gtmLoaded=true;
      INTERACTION_EVENTS.forEach(function(e){
        document.removeEventListener(e,onInteract,{passive:true,capture:true});
      });
      var f=document.getElementsByTagName('script')[0];
      var j=document.createElement('script');
      j.async=true;
      j.src='https://www.googletagmanager.com/gtm.js?id={{ settings.gtm_container_id | default: "GTM-58KH82X" }}';
      f.parentNode.insertBefore(j,f);
    }
    function onInteract(){ loadGTM(); }
    window.dataLayer.push({'gtm.start':new Date().getTime(),event:'gtm.js'});
    // Conversion-critical page types — load GTM immediately on DOMContentLoaded
    // to ensure session context is captured before any funnel events fire.
    var pageType = {{ request.page_type | json }};
    var CONVERSION_PAGES = ['product','collection','cart','index'];
    var isConversionPage = CONVERSION_PAGES.indexOf(pageType) !== -1;
    function scheduleGTM(){
      if(isConversionPage){
        // Load immediately — do not defer on conversion-critical pages
        loadGTM();
        return;
      }
      // Non-conversion pages: 3-tier idle strategy
      INTERACTION_EVENTS.forEach(function(e){
        document.addEventListener(e,onInteract,{passive:true,capture:true,once:true});
      });
      if('requestIdleCallback' in window){
        requestIdleCallback(loadGTM,{timeout:4000});
      } else {
        setTimeout(loadGTM,4000);
      }
    }
    if(document.readyState==='loading'){
      document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded',scheduleGTM);
    } else {
      scheduleGTM();
    }
  })();
  </script>

  {%- comment -%}── 8. META / SEO / FAVICON ──────────────────────────────────{%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if settings.favicon != blank -%}
    <link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="{{ settings.favicon | image_url: width: 32, format: 'webp', height: 32 }}">
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- render 'seo-meta' -%}
  {%- render 'lb-param-noindex' -%}
  {%- render 'lb-hreflang' -%}
  {%- render 'seo-schema' -%}

  {%- comment -%}── 9. CRITICAL CSS (inline) ──────────────────────────────────
    Covers header layout + hero dimensions so the first paint renders
    correctly before chaos-theme-styles.css and base.aio.min.css arrive.
    Keeping this here (not in stylesheets.liquid) makes the critical path
    explicit and easy to audit.
    All rules are minified — whitespace has real cost on slow connections.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- render 'stylesheets' -%}

  {%- comment -%}── 10 + 11. FONTS ────────────────────────────────────────────
    fonts.liquid: body_regular (woff2 preload + @font-face swap)
                  heading_font/Bebas Neue (woff2 preload, fetchpriority=low — queues after poster)
    lb-bebas-neue: product RTE typography styles (font loading removed in v1.1.0)
    Two preloads active (visual-clarity pass, Jul 2026) — fetchpriority=low on
    heading keeps it from competing with the 18.6KB hero poster on slow 4G.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- render 'fonts' -%}
  {%- render 'lb-bebas-neue' -%}

  {%- comment -%}── 12. THEME FLASH PREVENTION ────────────────────────────────
    Reads localStorage('lb-theme') and sets data-theme on <html> before
    first paint so dark/light mode never flashes the wrong theme.
    Zero network cost — pure JS with a try/catch for private browsing.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <script>
  (function(){
    try{
      document.documentElement.setAttribute(
        'data-theme',
        localStorage.getItem('lb-theme')||'light'
      );
    }catch(e){}
  })();
  </script>

  {%- comment -%}── 13. CSS CUSTOM PROPERTIES + COLOR SCHEMES ────────────────
    theme-styles-variables: CSS vars for spacing, typography, layout
    color-schemes: per-section color tokens (background, text, border)
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- render 'theme-styles-variables' -%}
  {%- render 'color-schemes' -%}

  {%- comment -%}── 14. NON-CRITICAL CSS (preload-swap / async) ───────────────
    All three stylesheets use the preload-swap pattern:
      rel="preload" as="style" onload="this.rel='stylesheet'"
    This means they download in parallel but do NOT block rendering.
    The critical-css.liquid inline block (step 9) covers all layout rules
    needed for first paint, so deferred arrival is a no-op re-apply.
    noscript fallbacks ensure CSS loads for users with JS disabled.

    Load order within this group:
      1. chaos-theme-styles.css  — theme base (largest, needs most lead time)
      2. lb-cart-ui.css          — cart drawer styles
      3. lb-pdp-buttons.css      — ATC + dynamic checkout (product + homepage)
      4. lb-variant-selectors.css — variant pills (product + homepage)
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <link rel="preload" href="{{ 'chaos-theme-styles.css' | asset_url }}" as="style" onload="this.onload=null;this.rel='stylesheet';">
  <noscript><link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ 'chaos-theme-styles.css' | asset_url }}"></noscript>

  <link rel="preload" href="{{ 'lb-cart-ui.css' | asset_url }}" as="style" onload="this.onload=null;this.rel='stylesheet';">
  <noscript><link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ 'lb-cart-ui.css' | asset_url }}"></noscript>

  {%- if template.name == 'product' or template.name == 'index' -%}
  <link rel="preload" href="{{ 'lb-pdp-buttons.css' | asset_url }}" as="style" onload="this.onload=null;this.rel='stylesheet';">
  <noscript><link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ 'lb-pdp-buttons.css' | asset_url }}"></noscript>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- if template.name == 'product' or template.name == 'index' -%}
  <link rel="preload" href="{{ 'lb-variant-selectors.css' | asset_url }}" as="style" onload="this.onload=null;this.rel='stylesheet';">
  <noscript><link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ 'lb-variant-selectors.css' | asset_url }}"></noscript>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- if template.name == 'collection' or template.name == 'search' -%}
  <link rel="preload" href="{{ 'lb-collection.css' | asset_url }}" as="style" onload="this.onload=null;this.rel='stylesheet';">
  <noscript><link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ 'lb-collection.css' | asset_url }}"></noscript>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- if template.name == 'product' -%}
  <link rel="preload" href="{{ 'lb-product-page.css' | asset_url }}" as="style" onload="this.onload=null;this.rel='stylesheet';">
  <noscript><link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ 'lb-product-page.css' | asset_url }}"></noscript>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- comment -%}── 15. VIEW TRANSITIONS (guarded) ───────────────────────────
    <link rel="expect" href="#MainContent"> explicitly gates rendering
    until #MainContent is parsed. Only inject when transitions are active
    in theme settings — do not leave it in unconditionally.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- comment -%}── 15. VIEW TRANSITIONS ─────────────────────────────────────
    blocking="render" and <link rel="expect"> removed — both prevented first
    paint until the script executed / <main> was parsed, causing severe LCP
    regression on mobile. view-transitions.js now loads with defer, which
    allows the page to render immediately while the script downloads.
    Cross-document transitions still work; the initial page load is no longer
    gated on the transition script.
  {%- endcomment -%}

  {%- comment -%}── 16. THEME EDITOR (design mode only) ──────────────────────{%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if request.design_mode -%}{%- render 'theme-editor' -%}{%- endif -%}

  {%- comment -%}── 17. MODULE IMPORTMAP + MODULEPRELOAD HINTS ────────────────
    scripts.liquid emits:
      - <script type="importmap"> for all theme ES modules
      - <link rel="modulepreload"> for hot-path modules (utilities, component,
        section-renderer, section-hydration, morph)
      - <script type="module"> lazy loads at fetchpriority=low for all
        non-critical modules (product-card, variant-picker, media-gallery…)
      - Template-conditional preloads (collection/search: paginated-list)
      - idleScripts array loaded via requestIdleCallback (accordion, slideshow…)
    All module scripts have fetchpriority="low" — they never compete with
    the LCP image or critical CSS.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- render 'scripts' -%}

  {%- comment -%}── 18–21. PERFORMANCE SAFETY NETS ───────────────────────────
    lb-app-css-defer:     MutationObserver catches runtime-injected app CSS
                          (Klaviyo popups) and defers via print swap.
                          Runs inline in <head> — must be here, not in <body>.
    lb-ghost-code-auditor: Dev-mode only — logs unused Shopify app scripts.
    lb-speculation-rules: Speculation Rules API — prefetch/prerender product
                          and collection pages on link hover (Chrome 109+).
                          Graceful no-op in unsupported browsers.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- render 'lb-app-css-defer' -%}
  {%- if settings.enable_dev_tools -%}{%- render 'lb-ghost-code-auditor' -%}{%- endif -%}
  {%- render 'lb-speculation-rules' -%}

</head>

<body class="page-width-{{ settings.page_width }} card-hover-effect-{{ settings.card_hover_effect }}">

  <a class="lb-skip-link" href="#MainContent">Skip to main content</a>

  {%- comment -%}── GTM NOSCRIPT (required by Google, must be first in <body>) ─
    Gated out of theme editor / visual preview so editor renders never log a
    GTM noscript hit. Customer renders are unaffected.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- unless request.design_mode or request.visual_preview_mode -%}
  <noscript>
    <iframe src="https://www.googletagmanager.com/ns.html?id={{ settings.gtm_container_id | default: "GTM-58KH82X" }}"
            height="0" width="0" style="display:none;visibility:hidden"
            title="Google Tag Manager"></iframe>
  </noscript>
  {%- endunless -%}

  {%- comment -%}── SKIP LINK ────────────────────────────────────────────────{%- endcomment -%}
  {%- render 'skip-to-content-link', href: '#MainContent', text: 'accessibility.skip_to_text' -%}

  {%- comment -%}── HEADER ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    Header CSS variables (--header-group-height, --top-row-height,
    --transparent-header-offset-boolean) are set via rAF to avoid
    forced synchronous layout reads during parse.
    The header-group div is pre-sized via critical CSS (min-height:80px)
    so there is no CLS before JS runs.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div id="header-group">
    {%- sections 'header-group' -%}
  </div>

  <script>
  // Header CSS var measurement — deferred to rAF so reads happen after
  // the browser has completed its first layout pass. This eliminates the
  // forced synchronous layout (FSL) that previously blocked the main thread
  // during HTML parse.
  requestAnimationFrame(function(){
    var hg  = document.getElementById('header-group');
    var hc  = hg && hg.querySelector('header-component');
    if(!hg || !hc) return;

    var bs = document.body.style;

    // ── Header group height (announcement bars above the header) ──
    var groupH = 0;
    for(var i=0,c=hg.children;i<c.length;i++){
      var el=c[i];
      if(el===hc||el.contains(hc)||!(el instanceof HTMLElement))continue;
      groupH+=el.offsetHeight;
    }
    bs.setProperty('--header-group-height', groupH+'px');

    // ── Top row height ──
    var topRow = hc.querySelector('.header__row--top');
    if(topRow) bs.setProperty('--top-row-height', topRow.offsetHeight+'px');

    // ── Transparent header offset ──
    var headerSection = hg.querySelector('.header-section');
    if(!headerSection || !hc.hasAttribute('transparent')){
      bs.setProperty('--transparent-header-offset-boolean','0');
      return;
    }
    var nextSection = headerSection.nextElementSibling;
    var hasImmediate = nextSection && nextSection.classList.contains('shopify-section');
    bs.setProperty('--transparent-header-offset-boolean', hasImmediate ? '0' : '1');
  });

  // ── Menu style detection (drawer vs inline) ──
  // Runs synchronously — no layout read, just feature detection.
  (function(){
    var hc = document.getElementById('header-component')
          || document.querySelector('header-component');
    if(!hc) return;
    var touch = 'ontouchstart' in window && navigator.maxTouchPoints > 0;
    var ol    = hc.querySelector('overflow-list');
    hc.dataset.menuStyle = (touch || (ol && ol.hasAttribute('minimum-reached')))
      ? 'drawer'
      : 'menu';
  })();
  </script>

  {%- comment -%}── MAIN CONTENT ─────────────────────────────────────────────{%- endcomment -%}
  <main id="MainContent"
        class="content-for-layout"
        data-page-transition-enabled="{{ settings.page_transition_enabled }}"
        data-product-transition="{{ settings.transition_to_main_product }}"
        data-template="{{ template }}">
    {{ content_for_layout }}
  </main>

  {%- comment -%}── FOOTER ────────────────────────────────────────────────────{%- endcomment -%}
  <footer>
    {%- sections 'footer-group' -%}
  </footer>

  {%- comment -%}── MODALS ────────────────────────────────────────────────────{%- endcomment -%}
  {%- render 'search-modal' -%}
  {%- if settings.quick_add or settings.mobile_quick_add -%}
    {%- render 'quick-add-modal' -%}
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- comment -%}── LB CUSTOM SCRIPTS (just before </body>) ──────────────────
    Moved from <head defer> to end of <body> to eliminate parse cost
    during initial load. Script only activates after DOMContentLoaded
    so placement here is functionally identical to defer — with the bonus
    that it doesn't add to TBT during HTML head parse.
      lb-product-card-tap.js — iOS single-tap flash via touchstart
    NOTE: lb-theme-toggle.js removed 2026-05-22 — file never existed in
    assets/, causing a 404 + MIME-type console error on every page load.
    Dark/light mode is handled by <meta name="theme-color"> in <head>;
    header scroll is handled by HeaderComponent in header.js;
    scroll reveal is handled by lb-idle-defer [data-lb-defer="visible"].
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <script src="{{ 'lb-product-card-tap.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>

  {%- comment -%}── JUDGE.ME INTERSECTION OBSERVER ──────────────────────────────
    lb-judgeme-carousel-css: delays Judge.me widget init until the reviews
    section enters the viewport (400px rootMargin). Works in concert with
    chaos_unleashed_third_party_defer which holds the Judge.me script until
    first user interaction. Only fires on product templates where the reviews
    widget is present. No-op on all other templates.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if template.name == 'product' -%}
    {%- render 'lb-judgeme-carousel-css' -%}
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- comment -%}── IDLE DEFER (last — catches everything below-fold) ─────────
    lb-idle-defer runs after all content is in the DOM. It uses
    requestIdleCallback to load lb-video-optimizer, lb-cart-animations,
    lb-image-optimizer and to activate [data-lb-defer] elements.
    Must be last in <body> — placing it earlier reduces the pool of
    elements it can observe on first run.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- render 'lb-idle-defer' -%}

  {%- comment -%}── SVG SPRITE (deferred to end of body) ──────────────────────
    Moved from top of body to end. SVG symbols are resolved during layout
    (after full DOM parse), so they work regardless of position in the
    document. Placing them here removes ~60KB of SVG parse cost from the
    critical rendering path, letting the browser reach LCP content sooner.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- render 'lb-svg-sprite' -%}

  {%- render 'lb-ga4-events' -%}
</body>
</html>
